<onlyinclude>'''Sensory processing''' is the transformation and organization of signals from sensory receptors and neural pathways. It allows organisms to respond to features such as light, sound, touch, body position and chemicals.

== Explanation ==
A receptor converts a stimulus into an electrical or chemical change. Neural pathways then transmit and transform signals, sometimes combining information from different senses. Perception is the resulting interpretation of sensory information; receptor activity alone does not establish conscious awareness.

